 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "A house for «آووا», light for the reward, hands for «وأولو الأرحام», geometric for «إن الله بكل شيء عليم». Paradise only named in the recitation; Al-Muyassar's «جنات النعيم» and As-Sa'di's «اتبعهم بإحسان» (Quran wording) not used. STAGING v4: c1 (74): inside a home by day. Three believers come in on 74:3 (the emigrants who left their homes; footsteps plate ending before the Name); their striving is not pictured. On 74:8 the three seated hosts (the helpers) rise and go to meet them, under a door plate for the shelter (74:9) and hand them a purse on 74:10 (Al-Muyassar: they sheltered them and shared with them wealth and support); both groups sit together on 74:13-14 (the true believers). The reward (74:15-18; both tafsirs: forgiveness and generous provision, in the Gardens) is only a light plate (74:15) with the camera wide (no close-up on the emigrants after the purse, so the provision does not read as the helpers' gift): nothing literal for Paradise, no gold, jewel or river. c2 (75): a town by day with the emigrants (left) and the helpers (centre); three later believers walk in from the right on 75:5 (those who believed and emigrated afterwards) under a footsteps plate and step to the others on 75:9 (they are of you: same rights and duties). Kinship (75:10-17; Al-Muyassar: inheritance between relatives) is a house plate only: no family or inheritance is acted. A geometric plate on the Name for All-Knowing (75:17). Every place on stage is filled."
 },
